ORIGIN
------

The engineering content of this project is derived from lecture material for:

    SEN102/212 Software Engineering Process
    Department of Software Engineering
    Obafemi Awolowo University, Ile-Ife, Nigeria

Lecturers whose material informs this work:
    Dr (Mrs) Onifade M. T.
    F. C. Ugwu
    Ubochi Chibueze Nmamouh

The complete original lecture deck is included in this repository under source/
for reference and attribution. Copyright in that material remains with its
authors and with Obafemi Awolowo University. It is included here for
educational reference and attribution, not as a claim of ownership.

The structure built on top of that material, being the kernel, the constitution,
the gate system, the agent fleet, the protocols, the instruments, the refusal
protocol, the mode system, the ledger specification and the tooling, is original
work by the Ìlànà contributors and is MIT licensed.

STANDARDS REFERENCED
--------------------

Ìlànà refers to the following standards. It reproduces neither their text nor
their normative content; it describes how to work in conformance with them.

    ISO/IEC 12207   Software Life Cycle Processes
    ISO/IEC 25010   Systems and software Quality Requirements and Evaluation
    IEEE 830        Software Requirements Specifications
    IEEE 1016       Software Design Descriptions
    IEEE 829        Software Test Documentation
    CMMI            Capability Maturity Model Integration (SEI, Carnegie Mellon)
    ACM/IEEE        Software Engineering Code of Ethics and Professional Practice

CMMI is a registered mark of Carnegie Mellon University. Ìlànà produces
indicative self-assessments using CMMI vocabulary; it does not perform, and its
output does not constitute, a formal SEI appraisal.

